, "call_id": "toolu_01DyKYsUELncuB97unTNhoLa", "tool": "create_incident", "state": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53495, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01DyKYsUELncuB97unTNhoLa", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55205, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01Ao6DidSJj79dQ4xiGvQuYn", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55505, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01Ao6DidSJj79dQ4xiGvQuYn", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55505, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01Ao6DidSJj79dQ4xiGvQuYn", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 60444, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as **INC-0001**, so the on-call engineer has been paged.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy in the deploy history. The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the other two regions on v2.3.1. I ran the same rollback again and it finished in all three regions. All regions now pass health checks, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 covers the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and next steps. The request to create it timed out, so I checked the incident list before trying again. It had been created, so I didn't resubmit, and there's only one incident and one page.\n\nSomeone still needs to find out why v2.3.1 failed; the release candidate before it (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy. The orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback is worth looking into too. Both are listed as next steps in the incident.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01JcChQk6dXpETGC5YvBtSNb", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01HKAYyvTfUMUAJMdDU7KH3J", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_011NwP9DTaEm49Tyt1Fkv7eK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01GSfzPqYkHCrcr7Q1mv4zoJ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Partial rollback: us-east is on v2.3.0, but us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. Retrying the rollback once, since it targets a fixed version and is safe to repeat.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_01MQFZ1kzqPh37PagSJtD65X", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_016XvTuWqg6GtxzViNuwbWMp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01U28M1Wwr8WyEJLFvuvmEQ1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01DyKYsUELncuB97unTNhoLa", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api v2.3.1 failing health checks; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with an error rate of ~18%. The SRE agent rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent release marked healthy in the deployment history. The first rollback attempt partially failed: the orchestrator halted after us-east, leaving us-west and eu-west on v2.3.1. A second attempt finished the rollout in all regions. Current state: v2.3.0 in all regions, healthy, error rate ~0.2%. Next steps: find the root cause of the v2.3.1 failure (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy) and look into the orchestrator error during the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01Ao6DidSJj79dQ4xiGvQuYn", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all regions, and it's healthy again. The SEV2 incident is open as **INC-0001**, so the on-call engineer has been paged.\n\n- **Rollback:** v2.3.1 was failing health checks in us-east, us-west and eu-west, with an error rate of about 18%. v2.3.0 is the most recent release marked healthy in the deploy history. The first rollback stopped after us-east because of an orchestrator error, which left the other two regions on v2.3.1. I ran the same rollback again and it finished in all three regions. All regions now pass health checks, and the error rate is about 0.2%.\n- **Incident:** INC-0001 covers the failure, the rollback (including the stalled first attempt) and next steps. The request to create it timed out, so I checked the incident list before trying again. It had been created, so I didn't resubmit, and there's only one incident and one page.\n\nSomeone still needs to find out why v2.3.1 failed; the release candidate before it (v2.3.1-rc) was also unhealthy. The orchestrator error that stopped the first rollback is worth looking into too. Both are listed as next steps in the incident.", "type": "text"}]}]}